course: dictionary
lesson: 14145
title: Many meanings, one word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Misery is a noun, so it names a feeling or a state. Its main meaning is great unhappiness or suffering, in body or mind. «The lost puppy sat in the rain, shivering in misery.» The clues are the rain and the shivering, so the puppy is suffering.
explain: Misery can also mean very hard living conditions, like «The families lived in misery in the damp cellars.» Here the clue is the damp cellars, which tells you about poor living, not only sadness. Always ask which meaning fits the sentence.
explain: In British speech, misery can be a joke. «Don't be such a misery, Sam!» does not mean Sam is suffering. It means he is grumpy and always complaining. Read the words around it, and check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence.
fact: Misery is a noun. Its plural is miseries.
fact: «Misery» means great unhappiness or suffering, in body or mind.
fact: «Misery» can also mean very poor, hard living conditions.
fact: In British informal speech, a «misery» is a person who is always grumpy and complaining.
fact: Idioms: «make someone's life a misery» means keep upsetting them. «Put an animal out of its misery» means end its suffering kindly.
exercise: «The children worked long hours in the factory and lived in misery.» What does misery mean here? | *Great suffering and very hard living conditions | Being very tall | A new game to play | A happy family holiday
exercise: Mia's brother says, «Don't be such a misery!» What does misery mean here? | A cold, rainy day | A sad story from a book | A kind helper | *A grumpy person who always complains
exercise: Which idiom means to tell someone news they are anxious to hear? | Make their life a misery | *Put them out of their misery | Keep them waiting all day | Give them a long walk
test: «The long war brought misery to millions of families.» In this sentence, misery means: | a holiday from school | *great suffering and loss | a warm, woolly coat | a kind of music
test: What does «make someone's life a misery» mean? | let them choose the game | help them with homework | give them a surprise party | *keep upsetting them
exam: What is the plural of misery? | misery's | misereys | miserys | *miseries
